## Prerequisites

- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) 24 or later
- A [Cloudflare account](https://dash.cloudflare.com/sign-up)

## Getting started

```bash
# Install dependencies, including the cf CLI
npm install

# Authenticate with Cloudflare (first time only)
npx cf login

# Generate the Env type from your bindings
npm run types
{{D1_LOCAL_SECTION}}
# Start the local development server
npm run dev
```

{{D1_LOCAL_SECTION_START}}
### Database setup

This project uses Cloudflare D1 with [Drizzle ORM](https://orm.drizzle.team/).

Create the database and copy its id into `cloudflare.config.ts`:

```bash
npx cf d1 create <database-name>
```

Then apply the migrations to your local simulation:

```bash
npm run db:migrate:local
```

To change the schema, edit `src/db/schema.ts` and generate a new migration:

```bash
npm run db:generate
npm run db:migrate:local
```
{{D1_LOCAL_SECTION_END}}

## Deployment

```bash
npm run deploy
```

{{D1_DEPLOY_SECTION_START}}
That runs two steps in order:

1. **`deploy:db`** — applies D1 migrations to the remote database
2. **`deploy:cf`** — builds and uploads the Worker

The database is migrated first so the deployed code never meets a schema it predates.
{{D1_DEPLOY_SECTION_END}}
{{NO_D1_DEPLOY_SECTION_START}}
That builds and uploads the Worker with `cf deploy`.
{{NO_D1_DEPLOY_SECTION_END}}

